WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.690
Ten years after Revenge of the Sith, Obi-Wan
Kenobi is readying a rematch with Darth Vader.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.940
"Hello there."

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.200
It's a good time to be a "Star Wars" fan.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.700
After the one-two punch of "The Mandalorian"
Seasons 1 and 2, followed by "The Book of

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.650
Boba Fett," Disney isn't letting up.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:25.160
It's only a short wait until May 25th, the
day "Obi-Wan Kenobi" lands on Disney+, with

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.240
the lead role reprised once more by Ewan McGregor.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.410
He will be joined by his former castmate Hayden
Christensen, who returns as Anakin Skywalker,

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.370
now known as Darth Vader.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.480
Even more "Star Wars: Episode III – Revenge
of the Sith" alums are along for the ride

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:45.100
as Joel Edgerton and Bonnie Piesse return
to their roles as Owen and Beru Lars, Luke

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.560
Skywalker's uncle and aunt.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.640
It even appears Jimmy Smits may return as
the Senator from Alderaan, Bail Organa.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:57.590
In terms of new faces, comedian and "Eternals"
star Kumail Nanjiani is on board in a still-unknown

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.590
role.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:02.750
"Game of Thrones" alumna Indira Varma and
Moses Ingram of "The Queen's Gambit" fame

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:07.250
had similarly secretive roles until the new
teaser trailer dropped on March 9th.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.780
The sneak peek at the original series reveals
Varma is playing an Imperial officer, and

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.970
Ingram will be playing the role of Reva, an
Imperial Inquisitor.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:20.720
With so many characters from the prequel trilogy
making their return amidst so many new faces,

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.760
many fans have wondered when, exactly, "Obi-Wan
Kenobi" takes place and how it fits into the

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.340
larger "Star Wars" timeline.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.049
As it turns out, those questions have quite
intriguing answers.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.690
Despite so much about the show being shrouded
in Sith-like secrecy, we still know a lot

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:39.840
about where "Obi-Wan Kenobi" fits into the
history of "Star Wars."

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.150
"That's good news."

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:46.330
"Obi-Wan Kenobi" will take place about 10
years after the rise of the Empire in "Revenge

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.650
of the Sith," as confirmed by a tweet from
the official "Star Wars" Twitter account from

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.909
December 2020.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:57.640
To date, the Disney+ "Star Wars" shows have
primarily focused on the post-Imperial era.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.450
Both "The Mandalorian" and "The Book of Boba
Fett" are set in the years after the death

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:06.350
of Emperor Palpatine in "Star Wars: Episode
VI – Return of the Jedi," so it will be

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.370
fascinating to finally see a story that takes
place during the height of Imperial power.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.370
Based on what we've seen in trailers and from
casting announcements, "Obi-Wan Kenobi" will

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:20.109
follow its titular character as he watches
over a young Luke Skywalker (and perhaps a

00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:21.700
young Leia) from afar.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:26.219
It appears the Clone Wars general is being
pursued by Imperial forces all the while,

00:02:26.219 --> 00:02:31.700
including several red-lightsaber toting figures
who appear to be Imperial Inquisitors.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:36.209
These are Force-sensitive hunters tasked with
exterminating the last of the Jedi Order,

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:39.560
led by the former Jedi known now as the Grand
Inquisitor.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.379
It appears the Empire is still busy hunting
down those who managed to save themselves

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:47.790
after Order 66 and will stop at nothing to
purge the galaxy of them.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:53.040
Obi-Wan is sure to be a major target in their
campaign, especially since Hayden Christensen

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.250
is slated to return as Darth Vader.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:59.170
Something tells us he's not going to let his
former master slip off into the twin sunsets

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.629
of Tatooine so easily.

00:03:00.629 --> 00:03:03.389
"I'm getting too old for this sort of thing."

00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:07.419
The final act of "Revenge of the Sith" ends
with Obi-Wan Kenobi witnessing the birth of

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:11.099
Padmé Amidala's newborn twins, Luke and Leia.

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:15.150
After Padmé dies in childbirth, a decision
is made to separate the twins and keep them

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.150
in hiding.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.969
Senator Organa and his wife become the adoptive
parents of Leia, who will grow up on Alderaan.

00:03:20.969 --> 00:03:25.939
Meanwhile, Luke is destined to grow up on
Tatooine, where Ewan McGregor's Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.139
leaves him in the care of Owen and Beru Lars.

00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:33.739
"Star Wars: Episode IV – A New Hope" takes
place 19 years after "Revenge of the Sith,"

00:03:33.739 --> 00:03:38.019
which means Luke and Leia are also 19 years
old when the original "Star Wars" trilogy

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:39.180
kicks off.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.540
This puts Disney+ limited series "Obi-Wan
Kenobi" almost smack in the middle of the

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.359
two films in regard to the "Star Wars" timeline.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:50.400
This is seemingly confirmed by the brief shot
of what appears to be a young Luke, who looks

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.749
to be nine or 10 years old, in the new teaser
trailer.

00:03:53.749 --> 00:03:58.879
Raised by Uncle Owen and Aunt Beru, Luke is
seen through Obi-Wan's futuristic binoculars

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:02.180
living on their moisture farm and pretending
to podrace.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.360
This may be a deliberate callback to "Star
Wars: Episode I – The Phantom Menace," in

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.189
which a much younger Obi-Wan meets a much
younger Anakin, also a podracer, on that same

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:12.579
sandy planet.

00:04:12.579 --> 00:04:16.920
Being set nine years before "A New Hope" also
means that "Obi-Wan Kenobi" happens around

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:22.500
the time of the events of "Solo: A Star Wars
Story," which follows a young Han Solo, Lando

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.950
Calrissian, and Chewbacca.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:28.820
It's unlikely that Obi-Wan will cross paths
with any of those characters, both because

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:33.390
none of the "Solo" actors have been cast in
"Obi-Wan Kenobi" and because the Jedi-in-hiding

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.700
doesn't meet Han Solo until the cantina scene
in "A New Hope."

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.970
Still, it's thrilling for fans to finally
see the years between the prequels and the

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.060
original trilogy explored in such depth.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.410
"Always on the move.”

